WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-23, with W8 (0.1.2)


STATE

  Version 0.1.2, Phase P2 (regular POSIX builtins), on branch dev.
  It adds:
  - command hash table (src/hash.c) with automatic invalidation on PATH
    changes (var.c path_gen), integrated with external command lookup in
    src/exec.c, plus the hash builtin (-r, list, lookup);
  - alias table (src/alias.c) with alias and unalias (-a), plus POSIX
    command-position alias expansion in input.c/lex.c/parse.c with
    bounded recursion prevention (TC_ALIAS_DEPTH_MAX) and trailing-blank
    chaining;
  - test and [ (src/bi_test.c) with exact POSIX 0..4-arg disambiguation,
    bounded recursive-descent for 5+ args (-o, -a, !, parens), file,
    string, and checked 64-bit integer primaries;
  - printf (src/bi_printf.c) with format reuse, width/precision/*,
    %b/\c/\0ddd, 'c char constants, numeric/float conversions, and %q;
  - echo (-n only, no backslash escapes by default), pwd (-L/-P),
    umask (octal and symbolic -S), read (-r, -d, bytewise stdin, IFS
    splitting, default REPLY), kill (-l, -s, -SIG, refusing %job), and
    ulimit (-H/-S/-a and resource flags) in src/builtins_io.c;
  - getopts (OPTIND/OPTARG, silent mode, explicit args), command
    (-p/-v/-V, function bypass, suppressing special-builtin fatal exit),
    and type in src/builtins_cmd.c;
  - sandbox/demo-0.1.2-builtins added to sandbox/play.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0; FUNCNEST sets the function recursion limit; signed
  64-bit arithmetic overflow is a reported error; echo recognizes -n only
  and does not interpret backslash escapes by default.


